## How the obligations are met (`stage-3/src/`)

| Obligations | Where / how |
|---|---|
| S3-010…012, D3-16, D3-17 | `store.stateFromFixture`: `created_at` on payments and authorizations (RFC 3339, and a future value gives 422); `setOpenings()`; seeded hold lifecycle and `closed_at` per D3-17. `/activity` sorts by `created_at`, with insertion order breaking ties. |
| S3-020…023, S3-053, D3-07, D3-14, D3-15, D3-20 | `ledger.parseInstant` parses strict RFC 3339 with an offset to BigInt nanoseconds. `instantParam()` gives 422 on an invalid or empty value and echoes the decoded text exactly. `ledger.totalAt`/`heldAt` compute the view, and `/me` returns all four fields for the same (A, K). |
| S3-030…036, S3-054, D3-08, D3-12, D3-19 | `app.buildStatement`: the selected revision per payment, the window `[from, to)` with `to` defaulting to the end of the request's millisecond, order by `(effective_at, id)` in code-unit order, the opening before `from`, and running `balance_after`. The entry `payment` is the original representation with `amount` set to the selected amount. |
| S3-060…065, D3-09, D3-10 | Every first read stores its full frozen result under an opaque `st_…` token (`state.snapshots`, exported, cleared by reset). A snapshot page accepts only `limit` and `offset`, and gives 422 with `from`, `to` or `known_at`. |
| S3-040…052, S3-055, D3-01…06, D3-11, D3-21 | `app.createCorrection`:<br>• checks run in D3-01 order;<br>• `recorded_at` = max(now, previous + 1 ms);<br>• the difference moves between the same two wallets;<br>• `ledger.overdraws` nets each instant and checks total and available at every past boundary (≤ now), for both parties, under the latest revisions with the proposed one substituted, and rejects only a new or deeper negative (D3-21).<br>`listRevisions` serves the revision history to the two parties. |
| S3-070, S3-071, S3-056 | A payment with a `settlement_id` or `authorization_id` gives 422 `linked_payment_immutable`. Settlement members are recorded at `committed_at`. |
| S3-080…085, S3-057 | `ledger.holdEvents`: creation +hold; each capture −amount at its payment time; the remainder is released at the `closed_at` of a final capture or void, or at `expires_at`. Expiry is known from the creation, so future views release open holds at their deadline. `closed_at` is set by `store.close()` and `sweep()`. |
| S3-072, D3-13, D3-18, D2-13 | `stateFromExport`:<br>• `schema` 1 or 2 imports get revision 1 at `created_at` and openings derived from the balances;<br>• a stage-2 voided hold closes at the import time, a captured one at its last capture, and an expired one at `expires_at`;<br>• schema 3 round-trips everything, including snapshots;<br>• stored responses replay byte for byte. |

## Known gaps, assumptions and risks

- **1→3 upgrade:** I did not run it against a real stage-1 container; only the schema-1 import path is exercised, in the tests. The adversary and auditor run the real XC for 1→3 and 2→3.
- **Statement reads store snapshots:** every first statement read stores a snapshot, which lasts until reset. Memory grows with the number of reads. That is acceptable for a test-reset lifecycle, but it is unbounded within one reset.
- **Historical cost is O(n) per read:** historical views and the overdraft check scan the user's payments and holds on every read. That is fine at test scale, but there is no index.
- **D3-18 and D3-21:** an imported stage-2 void releases at the import time. D3-21 keeps that approximation from blocking unrelated corrections.
- **Carried over from stages 1–2:**
  - in-memory state;
  - scrypt N=2^12;
  - a lost capture response is shown with the refusal style (the adversary's stage-2 observation).

